# Static analysis for the llvm-mos freezemenu. Run with `cmake --build build --target tidy`;
# it is expected to be clean, so read the exit status.
#
# The check list is deliberately narrow at the edges, because a 6502 target trips several checks
# that are sound advice on a hosted system and wrong here. Each exclusion below says why, so that
# nobody has to re-derive it — and so that adding one requires the same.
#
# The high-volume arithmetic advisories live in the separate `tidy-arithmetic` target rather than
# here: they are worth reading, but there are 187 of them and they would bury everything else.

Checks: >
  bugprone-*,
  clang-analyzer-*,
  performance-*,
  portability-*,
  readability-identifier-naming,
  readability-inconsistent-declaration-parameter-name,
  readability-braces-around-statements,
  readability-misleading-indentation,
  readability-non-const-parameter,
  readability-isolate-declaration,
  readability-redundant-control-flow,
  misc-*,

  -clang-analyzer-optin.core.FixedAddressDereference,
  -clang-analyzer-core.FixedAddressDereference,
  -clang-analyzer-core.NullDereference,
  -clang-analyzer-security.insecureAPI.strcpy,
  -clang-analyzer-security.insecureAPI.DeprecatedOrUnsafeBufferHandling,
  -performance-no-int-to-ptr,
  -bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters,
  -bugprone-signed-bitwise,
  -bugprone-implicit-widening-of-multiplication-result,
  -bugprone-narrowing-conversions,
  -misc-use-anonymous-namespace,
  -misc-include-cleaner,
  -misc-use-internal-linkage,
  -portability-avoid-pragma-once,
  -portability-no-assembler,

WarningsAsErrors: '*'

# This project's own headers, and only those. Without a filter clang-tidy reports through the SDK
# and mega65-libc headers, which are not ours to fix and which drown everything else.
#
# This has broken silently once already: an earlier value named files from a different project and
# matched nothing, so no header was ever checked. It broke the same way a second time when this
# repository split out of a parent tree that put these sources under llvm/src/ -- the prefix this
# value used to need -- and became its own repository with them at src/ instead. Same failure mode
# as the FixedAddressDereference rename above: a regex that stops matching produces silence, not an
# error, so absence of header findings is not by itself evidence the filter is working.
HeaderFilterRegex: 'src/[^/]+\.h$'

# Rust's naming, because that is what the rest of this repository is written in and there is no
# reason for the helper to read differently: types UpperCamelCase, functions and variables
# snake_case, constants SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE, enum variants UpperCamelCase.
CheckOptions:
  # Types: UpperCamelCase
  readability-identifier-naming.ClassCase: CamelCase
  readability-identifier-naming.StructCase: CamelCase
  readability-identifier-naming.EnumCase: CamelCase
  readability-identifier-naming.TypeAliasCase: CamelCase
  readability-identifier-naming.TypedefCase: CamelCase

  # Functions and variables: snake_case
  readability-identifier-naming.FunctionCase: lower_case
  readability-identifier-naming.MethodCase: lower_case
  readability-identifier-naming.VariableCase: lower_case
  readability-identifier-naming.ParameterCase: lower_case
  readability-identifier-naming.MemberCase: lower_case
  readability-identifier-naming.NamespaceCase: lower_case

  # Constants: SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE, and enum variants UpperCamelCase as in Rust.
  readability-identifier-naming.ConstantCase: UPPER_CASE
  readability-identifier-naming.ConstexprVariableCase: UPPER_CASE
  readability-identifier-naming.EnumConstantCase: CamelCase

  # A `let` binding in Rust is snake_case whether or not it can be rebound; only `const` and
  # `static` items shout. So a plain `const` local is an ordinary variable here, while a local
  # `constexpr` — the thing Rust spells `const` — is caught by the option above and shouts.
  readability-identifier-naming.LocalConstantCase: lower_case
  readability-identifier-naming.LocalConstantPointerCase: lower_case
  readability-identifier-naming.ConstantParameterCase: lower_case
  readability-identifier-naming.ConstantMemberCase: lower_case

# misc-no-recursion was excluded here as "nothing here recurses, and it fires through the SDK's
# templates". Both had stopped being true: the header filter now keeps the SDK out, and the check
# was the one thing that would have caught report_unmapped() calling itself. It reports zero on
# this tree, so it costs nothing to keep enforced.

# Why each exclusion:
#
#   clang-analyzer-optin.core.FixedAddressDereference
#   clang-analyzer-core.FixedAddressDereference
#       Dereferencing a fixed address is the entire job. $D020 is the border colour, not a wild
#       pointer. The SDK's own dma.hpp trips this too.
#
#       Both spellings are listed because the check's name moved between them: clang-tidy 23 has
#       it under `optin.core.`, clang-tidy 22 (CI's stock, unpatched SDK) still has it under
#       `core.`.  A renamed check fails silently -- an unknown name in this list is ignored, not
#       diagnosed -- so whichever spelling the running clang-tidy does not have simply matches
#       nothing, and the finding reappears as if unsuppressed.  Listing both covers either
#       direction of a toolchain change, not just a bump forward.
#
#   clang-analyzer-core.NullDereference
#       `POKE(0, 65)` and `POKE(0x01, 0x36)` are the 6510 port register at $00/$01 — the CPU port
#       that sets speed and banks ROM in and out. Address zero is a real, essential register here,
#       not a null pointer.
#
#   clang-analyzer-security.insecureAPI.strcpy
#   clang-analyzer-security.insecureAPI.DeprecatedOrUnsafeBufferHandling
#       Both want the Annex K `_s` functions, which this freestanding libc does not provide. There
#       is nothing to migrate to.
#
#   bugprone-signed-bitwise
#       752 findings, none actionable. C's integer promotions turn every `uint8_t` operand into a
#       signed `int` before any bitwise operator, so `CIA2.pra & 0xfc` — the ordinary shape of
#       hardware register code — fires. Suppressing it would mean a `U` suffix or a cast on every
#       mask in the program. The genuinely dangerous signed cases are shifts that overflow, and
#       those are what bugprone-implicit-widening-of-multiplication-result catches.
#
#   bugprone-implicit-widening-of-multiplication-result
#   bugprone-narrowing-conversions
#       Real and worth reading, but 187 findings between them, almost all provably-safe screen
#       arithmetic. They have their own target, `tidy-arithmetic`, so that `tidy` can stay clean
#       and therefore enforceable.
#
#   misc-use-internal-linkage
#       Wrong answers here, and no upside. It sees one translation unit, so it proposes `static`
#       for `charset` and `root_dir_sector`, which other files reach through their own `extern`
#       declarations — taking the advice would break the link. And there is nothing to gain:
#       llvm-nm shows LTO already giving these symbols local binding.
#
#   performance-no-int-to-ptr
#       Casting an integer to a pointer is how a memory-mapped register is reached. $D020 is the
#       border colour, and there is no other spelling of it.
#
#   bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters
#       copy(source, destination, count) and fill(destination, value, count) mirror the DMA
#       controller's own argument order. Renaming or wrapping them to satisfy the check would put
#       this code further from the hardware it describes, not closer.
#
#   misc-use-anonymous-namespace
#       `static` at file scope is what the llvm-mos optimisation guide asks for, and it is what
#       makes the single-translation-unit layout work when a test #includes the program.
#
#   misc-include-cleaner
#       Cannot see through the platform headers' own includes and asks for headers that do not
#       exist in this SDK.
#
#   portability-avoid-pragma-once
#       Only ever visible once the header filter above was fixed. There is one compiler here and
#       it supports `#pragma once`; include guards would trade a working line for a name to keep
#       unique. This was the only thing the broken filter had been hiding.
#
#   modernize-redundant-void-arg
#       Never enabled, and deliberately: it is a C++ check giving backwards advice in C. It
#       flags `int main(void)` and wants the `void` removed, but `f()` and `f(void)` are only
#       equivalent from C23 -- before that `f()` declares unspecified parameters and turns off
#       argument checking. The 107 sites it reports are the correct ones; the 34 written `f()`
#       were the defect, and are now `f(void)` too.
#
#   portability-no-assembler
#       A safety-critical coding-standard rule (no assembler at all). Inline asm is how this
#       program reaches the hypervisor and the 45GS02's own instructions; there is no C spelling
#       of them.
